{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.bc087f5d9fbd715608217546.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The assessment concerns one identified office and one identified set of services; all three facts refer to that same assessment.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.bc087f5d9fbd715608217546.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Applicable regulated-activity carve-outs have been resolved before supplying regulated_services.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.bc087f5d9fbd715608217546.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The requested result is satisfaction of Q3's stated three-factor trigger. It does not establish a complete statutory licensing determination.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.bc087f5d9fbd715608217546.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Business and territorial classifications incorporate professional assessment; unknown inputs remain unknown.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.bc087f5d9fbd715608217546.a4","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The required TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED label is used as a trigger flag only and does not imply that a licensed office's conduct is prohibited.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"773eda47be7f7e6881f9a66c1c5018e397af06d47b97a2ec6602f9f8384969f8","candidate_id":"candidate.fc1b0c83b4664b578657fd23f0b000d7","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] Selected control: Q3's three-factor licensing-trigger flag, after regulated-activity carve-outs are resolved. True means that regulated services, carrying on a business providing those services, and carrying on that business in Hong Kong are all established. False means this conjunction is not satisfied; it does not approve the office's conduct. The label does not assert an actual prohibition, absence of a licence, or whole-entity compliance.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["definitions"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":["issue.44cff453e7604e04be718eb071465686","issue.dc739b9979cd4a2c84bc25764eeb3f19","issue.c95f2723782e4b1aadde22d8832ada40","issue.2dc45083885d44ac80dff959732ee970","issue.88293b17830a4327bb590876c06303ef"],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"The express conjunction supports one formal reading of the selected trigger. The strongest uncertainty lies upstream in business classification: the ordinary-course sentence can be understood as coordinating absence of business operation and absence of a profit objective, or as making non-business operation an independent alternative because of 'or'. A genuine office receiving only expense reimbursements but pursuing profit exposes that difference: the first understanding withholds the ordinary-course expectation, while the second may support it. Neither wording establishes an automatic exemption or a definitive trigger outcome, so a rival Boolean formula would overstate the source.","run_id":"run.a35ca77c01a34a7db02e90b9015136e2","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"e7c3a71dc77ad1426f9f9ab7bc8f5b31438bca655a186478fa311d88d3e866ae","source_unit_ids":["daa1876316641.u18.26414","daa1876316641.u38.27681","daa1876316641.u39.28171","daa1876316641.u40.28601"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Q3 licensing trigger for the assessed family office and its services"}